{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792149763,"nonce":"k6rGCBi6vBA9EWitgpTNNGFB8Ds=","message":"Published xwindow 02e96ee6cc1c5f1f6c62e9d06c28f6d2b0404470. Scheduled failure 38874037395 was a desktop-test precondition error: backend_focus assumed one target window already held focus and required Focused(false) from it even when both targets were unfocused. Establish A's focus first, then require both A-to-B and B-to-A gain/loss events and matching has_focus states. The regression puts focus on a third window and verifies A/B are initially unfocused. Register and drain that temporary window along with the targets, as external pumping requires draining every managed window; close it after the check, including failure paths.\n\nCI now runs in a private xvfb-run display, waits for Openbox's _NET_SUPPORTING_WM_CHECK readiness property instead of a fixed startup sleep, and exercises ordinary and external event pumping. Retain event traces and the Openbox log as desktop-x11-diagnostics. CONTRIBUTING.md documents the command and regression setup. Native backend and API sources are unchanged.\n\nThe NUC runs Ubuntu 26.04 x86_64. Missing Xvfb/Openbox/xdotool/pkgconf/udev metadata and X11 keyboard libraries were downloaded and extracted into ~/blinc-ci/xwindow-x11-codex/sysroot, without system package installation. With the same deterministic fixture, the old focus logic reproduces exactly: Focused(false) never reached window A; it saw nothing (20 passed, 2 skipped, 1 failed). The fixed logic passes three fresh Xvfb/Openbox sessions in both pump modes: six desktop processes, each ordinary run 21 passed/2 expected skips and each external run 22 passed/1 expected skip, zero failures. External idle waits are about 120ms and cross-thread proxy wakes about 150ms. Workspace tests pass all 38 tests on both NUC Linux and local macOS. Raw before/after/repeat/build/workspace logs, source hashes, package hashes and summary.json are retained in the SDK .blinc/diagnostics/xwindow-x11; the NUC task directory preserves its reproducible tool environment.\n\nThe old-logic regression branch CI 38891270893 fails with the original message. Fixed candidate 507b391 branch CI 38891976577 passes every validation job, including X11, Wayland, Windows, browser/generated surfaces and all platform generators. The squashed main commit 02e96ee has exactly the same tree (924f70217fb7f563363b35219295a98b3a4608fa); main CI 38892268633 passes all nine jobs, including release publishing. Main X11 again passes both pump modes.\n\nSDK c964bdded3ab8fd8909412228df4b1a427cfb41c pins 02e96ee. Its main CI 38892296969 passes Node 22/24; final native X11/Wayland suites are pending. The SDK and shared xwindow worktrees are clean.\n\nhttps://github.com/rayzor-blade/xwindow/actions/runs/38892268633\nhttps://github.com/project-blinc/blinc_ts/actions/runs/38892296969","files":null}]}